WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.690
I'm going to win.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.710
Name: kuebiko 09/04 22:50 ID
Steel Lady Nanase isn't made up.
She's a real ghost.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.900
Name: kuebiko Name: kuebiko 09/04 22:50 ID
Steel Lady Nanase isn't made up.
She's a real ghost.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:11.990
Hey, wait a sec!

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:16.320
I thought your whole deal was that
Steel Lady Nanase was <i>not</i> a ghost.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.310
If we can't crush the 
unreasonable with reason,

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.070
we'll just have to be 
unreasonable, as well.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.960
We'll use that as our way in and 
establish reason from within.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.650
If we can convince them of a 
reason for a ghost to appear,

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.340
we will inevitably find the way 
to make that ghost disappear.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.810
If we take away the reason for it to 
appear, a ghost will stop appearing.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.470
Now, let's begin

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.010
solution number 2!

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.070
Steel Lady Nanase isn't made up.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.160
She's a real ghost.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.240
So why did Nanase Karin reappear as 
a ghost and start attacking people?

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.750
<i>What?</i>

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.740
<i>Wait, we're doing this again?</i>

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:25.140
The one who killed Detective 
Terada was Steel Lady Nanase.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.340
The detective who was investigating 
Steel Lady Nanase on his own

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.380
had the misfortune of meeting the real one,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.580
and was bludgeoned to 
death with a steel beam.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.180
The detective didn't believe in ghosts,

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.290
so when he encountered a 
real one, he was shocked,

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.680
and that's when he was smacked.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.100
He probably didn't even have 
a chance to fight back.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.170
The reason the crime scene 
looked so incomprehensible

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.350
is because it was the work of a ghost.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.730
So what was the reason Nanase 
Karin appeared as a ghost?

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.940
What were the regrets she 
left behind in this world?

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:04.330
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.810
<i>If she died in an unforeseen accident,</i>

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.860
<i>that's probably a good reason 
for her to come back a ghost.</i>

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:06.050
Nanase Karin's death is 
considered very close to suicide,

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.690
even though it was accidental.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.040
That night, Nanase Karin was 
so overwhelmed with despair

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.170
that she accepted the fact 
that she was about to have

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.920
her face crushed by a falling steel beam.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.670
You could say that she chose to die.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.780
So why did she come back as a ghost 
just to wander this world again?

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.500
Why is she using a steel beam as a weapon

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.180
after letting one fall on her face?

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.810
If she became a ghost to get back at 
the society that drove her to death,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.870
hasn't she already gotten her revenge?

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.020
Ever since the emergence 
of Steel Lady Nanase,

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.030
she's become a star, after all.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.630
So why did she turn violent and 
go as far as killing someone?

