00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.160
<b>Relevant Blogs</b>

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.160
<b>Links</b>

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.160
<b>Other Occult Forums</b>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.790
<b>Her Father's Accidental Death</b>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.790
<b>Nanase Karin was suspected of killing her father</b>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.790
<b>Nanase Karin's father died in June after she turned 19</b>

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.790
<b>He fell and hit his head after falling down the stairs of his apartm</b>

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.270
The reason she was chased out 
of the spotlight as an idol

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:54.290
is because she was suspected 
of killing her own father.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.570
At that point, even if she'd returned,

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.550
she'd only instill fear and 
receive more criticism.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.610
Therefore, the reason 
Nanase Karin became a ghost

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.550
wasn't her hatred toward society.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.780
She appeared because she 
wanted to tell the world

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.180
about a different problem 
and a different truth.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.890
And because the world just 
refused to understand her,

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.600
no matter how much time passed,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.730
she became violent.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.450
Just think about it.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:25.050
It's not like she'd been cleared 
of the suspicion of murder.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.910
If she had truly killed her father,

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.850
what would she be trying to 
tell the world right now?

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.160
She's enraged because she 
didn't kill her father.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.450
That's why she came back as a ghost. 
To tell everyone the truth.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.760
<b>Complaint</b>

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.760
But is that truly everything?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.510
Isn't her rage longing for something else?

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.000
This isn't a deduction.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:55.830
Correct.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.810
For the second solution, I am nothing 
more than a fiction writer.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.740
The readers here support 
and believe in ghosts.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:08.740
I'm going to solve this mystery and 
ritualistically make our ghost disappear.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.660
Let's return to the beginning.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.000
Why did Nanase Karin, an idol 
who only had a cult following,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.670
<b>Murder Allegations Surface
for a So-So Idol Suspected of Killing Her Own Father?!</b>

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.670
The idol with a flamethrower whose
popularity exploded with her late-night drama!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.170
face allegations of something as 
horrible as killing her father?

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.170
It was thought that her motive was her father's life insurance.
It was rumored that she didn't think very highly of her father, who was
unemployed. We were able to get confirmation from a former employee
at a talent agency.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:24.780
Someone had plotted against her 
and forged these allegations.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.040
Nanase Karin fell into a trap.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.060
That's why she reappeared as a ghost.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.810
Nanase Karin wants to protest against

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.850
the one who tricked her 
and drove her to suicide.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:43.070
We have to take what we know and find 
out the truth behind the allegations.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.690
Who was the first one to accuse 
her of killing her father?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.580
<i>What I'm about to say is a bit risky, but...</i>

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:58.750
It's none other than the one who 
was killed, Nanase Karin's father.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.900
Her father felt that she was going to kill him

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.500
and even left that in writing,

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:04.510
I think Haruko is trying to kill me.
I'm sure that by the time someone reads this, 
Haruko will have already killed me. I just know it.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.490
and that was discovered after his death.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.970
Could there be anything so convenient?

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.470
If Nanase Karin truly did push 
her father down the stairs

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.740
to make it seem like an accident,

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.660
she probably would've been worried about 
any handwritten notes or the like

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.730
and disposed of them immediately.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:26.060
And it's hard to believe that 
she would actually murder him

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.860
while he was telling others 
that he was wary of her.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.320
<i>It was said that Nanase Karin managed to</i>

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.300
<i>dodge investigations 
because she was so smart.</i>

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.710
<i>But she made a lot of 
mistakes if that's the case.</i>

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:40.240
<i>Well, when you lay it all out like that, 
a lot of it seems unthinkable.</i>

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.080
Correct.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.590
Nanase Karin didn't kill her father.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.710
She didn't even feel 
any malice toward him.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.090
So why did her father feel like she did?

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:53.420
The one who lured Nanase Karin 
into a trap was her own father.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.790
In order to ruin his daughter's success,

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.440
he killed himself in a way 
that would appear accidental

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.800
and made it so someone would 
find his handwritten thoughts

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.370
about his daughter's malice.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.860
<i>You know, this story could actually be true...</i>

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.660
One can only imagine what 
their relationship was like.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.850
There are reports that he quit working

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.950
because he wanted part of 
his daughter's earnings.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.410
She's making a fool of me.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.770
She's always rubbed her 
intelligence in my face.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.970
She's your daughter.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:31.020
How can you say such awful things 
about a nice girl like her? You're crazy.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:36.430
It's probably true that her father 
was wary of their relationship.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:40.230
He survived on his daughter's flashy job.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.730
But he also developed a complex because of it.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:47.440
He felt like he was suffering, 
but no one cared.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.150
That's what caused him 
to resent his daughter.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.150
Haruko

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.820
If he couldn't achieve the same 
amount of success as his daughter,

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.120
he would commit suicide 
and drag her down with him.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.620
That was the purpose of his death.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.210
I think Haruko is trying to kill me.
I'm sure that by the time someone reads this, 
Haruko will have already killed me. I just know it.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.210
It was his last show of pride.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.250
And to that end, he left behind a time bomb:

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.420
his handwritten note.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:12.590
And just like her father had planned, 
Nanase Karin was looked down upon.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:15.760
Nanase-san,

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:19.520
what did your father 
really mean in his note?

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.410
I don't know anything! 
Sorry, I'm in a hurry.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:23.230
Hey, wait!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.230
I mean, the note that your father 
left behind was pretty clear!

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.070
He said that you were going to kill him.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:30.830
Nanase-san!

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:37.630
That's what drove her into an 
accident that was near suicide.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.290
That's how Nanase Karin died.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.780
She died, and her soul moved 
on to the next world.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:56.760
And then, she reunited with 
her father, who died before her,

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.030
and heard the truth from his own mouth.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.940
"She heard the truth from his 
own mouth"?! Oh, come on!

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.570
Well, where else was she 
supposed to find out the truth?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.210
After finding out her own father 
maliciously tried to ruin her,

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:17.900
she became filled with regret, 
and her soul could not fully move on.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.370
That's why she came back to this world

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.210
and is trying to tell people the truth.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.170
She wanted people to know the tragedy

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.530
that she did not kill her father, 
but it was her father who killed her.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.830
That's why she's a ghost on a rampage.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:38.140
Nanase Karin turned evil because 
of her father's betrayal.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.990
She turned into an unsightly monster.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.060
If we pity her,

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:48.190
remember how beautiful she once was, 
and wish for her soul to move on in peace,

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:51.060
Steel Lady Nanase will probably 
disappear from our nights.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.030
The ones who can bring her peace are 
the ones who believe this story.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:04.680
All of you must be the judges!

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:08.380
Nanase Karin, AKA Nanase Haruko...

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:12.170
Let us lay her soul to rest with our prayers!

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.840
<b>Anon</b>

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.690
<i>Poor Karin-chan!</i>

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:20.260
<b>Nameless</b>

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:20.260
<i>That changes Steel Lady Nanase's image.</i>

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.930
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.930
<i>I sorta understand how 
her dad felt, though.</i>

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.730
They're so accepting of this, 
despite her talking about the afterlife...

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:57.210
Hey, I think she might 
actually be getting weaker.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.810
I'm pretty sure Rikka-san didn't 
predict that we would switch over

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:05.670
from such an orthodox solution to 
the complete opposite so quickly.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.410
I did try to convince people 
who want to believe in ghosts

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:12.590
that there was indeed a ghost.

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:15.230
That just meant they would 
support that even more.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:19.820
I think Kuro-senpai had an easier 
time choosing that reality, too.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.700
But this still doesn't ensure our victory.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:26.900
<i>I mean, I can totally see her own 
father setting a trap for her,</i>

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.130
<i>but you know...</i>

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:32.120
<i>Honestly, it just looks like she's 
wreaking havoc on the world.</i>

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.380
<i>She even killed a detective.</i>

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.550
Rikka-san has started to 
regain control of the flow.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:48.270
If Nanase Karin's ghost appeared more 
clearly and looked more spiteful,

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:51.880
we might've been able to conclude 
everything with the second solution.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.610
Regrettably, the name of 
Steel Lady Nanase is going to

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.400
<b>Steel Lady Nanase</b>

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:56.400
be a huge obstacle for us to overcome.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.860
It's hard to believe that a 
ghost who had valid complaints

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:02.990
or requests would wreak so much havoc.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:08.210
But Rikka-san wasn't able 
to completely deny my story.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:18.330
If we're going to continue choosing a story

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:22.300
that more people across the Internet 
want and are likely to believe,

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.690
Rikka-san will have to accept 
at least part of my story,

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.550
since it's been persuasive.

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:32.140
Besides, everyone looks forward 
to the minority with a disadvantage

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:37.580
completely turning the tables on the 
majority with a clear advantage.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.030
Now, on to...

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:44.410
our third solution.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:57.000
Dueling Fictions

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.230
Let's formulate another hypothesis.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.530
Steel Lady Nanase is not a spectre.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:07.890
She is a fake ghost created 
by a living human being,

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:11.350
and the one who killed Detective 
Terada is also human.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:14.950
Because Steel Lady Nanase 
is not Nanase Karin,

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:17.350
its appearance and her 
death don't match up.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:24.240
<b>Steel Lady Nanase Investigation Headquarters</b>

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.240
I'd like to revisit Nanase Karin's death.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.060
There are still some inconsistencies 
about her death.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.990
Nanase Karin
(Haruko)

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:27.990
<b>Dead</b>

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:31.700
There are those who say that 
didn't sound like a way she'd go.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.700
Accidental
Death

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:31.700
An accidental death
that seemed like suicide

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.910
She definitely felt trapped.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.330
She had lost her hard-earned place 
in the entertainment business,

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.540
and a comeback was proving difficult.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.840
On top of that, she was 
accused of killing her father.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.630
And if those accusations stemmed from 
her own father's handwritten notes,

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.980
then her whole life had 
basically been shattered.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.920
The motives for a suicide are all there.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:58.400
But her own older sister is expressing 
doubts about her suicide.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.730
Nanase Karin
(Haruko)

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.730
<b>Dead</b>

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.400
Nanase Karin
(Haruko)

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.400
Dead

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:58.400
Older Sister

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:03.900
<b>Anon</b>

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:00.840
<i>I heard the interview.</i>

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.900
<i>She said she didn't think that was 
enough to actually get to her sister,</i>

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:07.570
<i>and that she wouldn't willfully 
die such a gruesome death.</i>

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:09.780
When a family member commits suicide,

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.490
there are times when the remaining 
family members can't readily accept it.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:17.810
If part of the reason for that suicide 
is another family member,

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:22.040
they tend to shift the blame to someone 
else so they won't be suspected.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.300
But her sister made statements 
to the police and others

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.710
that just made them suspect her more.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:29.300
<b>Morgue</b>

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.850
Would she have said all that
just to shift the blame?

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.320
Her sister had doubts 
from the very beginning.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:43.210
Did Nanase Karin, 
AKA Nanase Haruko, truly die?

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:47.140
Couldn't it have been someone else 
that was crushed by the steel beam?

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:49.410
<i>A double?</i>

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:52.840
<i>A double is a given when you 
have a corpse without a face.</i>

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:56.450
Of course, they took the proper 
steps to identify the corpse.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.310
Her clothes, her blood type, 
her fingerprints,

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:00.830
her physical appearance...

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.880
But how trustworthy is any of that?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:05.840
Clothes can be changed.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:09.760
It's not like she had ever been 
fingerprinted by the police prior.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.860
You could always switch out

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.670
the personal belongings in her 
room with someone else's.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.540
Her teeth were smashed to 
pieces along with her face.

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:20.880
There are plenty of other people 
who have her blood type.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.230
You can't dismiss the possibility that
she'd been switched with someone else.

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:28.810
Which means it's theoretically 
possible to have a double.

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:30.780
Despite the fact that 
her face was smashed in,

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.990
if the police conclude that a double 
wasn't possible, it'd be a success.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:38.240
<b>Nameless</b>

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:38.240
<i>But realistically speaking, switching 
the bodies out would've been impossible.</i>

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:40.500
Reality doesn't matter.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:41.890
Older Sister

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.470
What's important is that 
Nanase Karin's older sister

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.020
Doubt

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:47.620
actually had suspicions that this 
corpse could've been someone else.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:48.170
Nanase Karin
(Haruko)

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.170
Older Sister

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.170
Doubt

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.170
Dead

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.170
Accidental Death

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.170
An accidental death
that seemed like suicide

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:51.800
Her younger sister died in 
a very uncharacteristic way.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:56.300
Her sassy little sister, who was smart and 
on the road to becoming a popular idol.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.680
There's no way she'd die like that.

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:01.560
Of course she'd think that way.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.690
Or rather...

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.300
The more spite you might've had yourself,

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:07.900
the more likely you are to suspect 
someone else doing the same.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.530
So who was the one who leaked her 
father's handwritten note to the media?

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.990
The only probable answer is 
Nanase Karin's older sister.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.830
Was Hatsumi actually fond 
of her little sister?

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:25.880
Surely, she was always unfairly 
compared to her glorious little sister.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:30.210
The sisters probably 
were not on good terms.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.440
When the allegations came out that 
Nanase Karin may have killed her father,

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:34.680
<b>Steel Lady Nanase Investigation Headquarters</b>

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:37.250
her sister never made any 
statements to defend her.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.180
Older Sister

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.180
Handwritten
note

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.180
Dad

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.180
Publisher

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.180
Doubt

