00:18:55.150 --> 00:19:04.330
Steel
Lady
Nanase

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:58.700
Most people wouldn't exactly feel at ease

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.100
if the ghost of a family member appeared,

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.330
but in Hatsumi's case, 
it was for the better.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:07.250
<i>So who would be the 
suspect in that case?</i>

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.850
<i>Hatsumi's boyfriend?</i>

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.330
The chances of that are low.

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:13.230
There's no way she wouldn't 
have noticed her boyfriend

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.300
doing strange things at night.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:21.860
The suspect had time on their hands and 
would do anything it took for Hatsumi.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:25.850
We can assume it was someone who was 
single and had deviant tendencies.

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:30.550
The suspect created a ghost named 
Steel Lady Nanase that never existed,

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:32.850
all of the sake of Nanase Karin's older sister,

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:35.860
then killed Detective Terada, 
whom he randomly encountered.

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:40.740
The suspect felt cornered after going 
so far as to murder someone for Hatsumi,

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:44.530
and might've wanted to further their 
relationship, going as far as to harm her.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.730
Steel Lady Nanase isn't a spectre.

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:53.830
We need to find this degenerate quickly

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:56.790
and confirm that everyone 
involved in this is safe.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.470
Are you all right?

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.060
